<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST - P&amp;U '96 EPS seen $1.92/share.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - P&amp;U '96 EPS seen $1.92/share.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/U.S. drugs group Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn (P&amp;U) was expected to post earnings per share (EPS) of $1.92 for 1996, a Reuters poll of 12 analysts found on Monday.</p>
<p>The forecast regards earnings before costs for the merger and for restructuring as well as other one-time items, which together are exepected to amount to $1 a share.</p>
<p>Forecasts varied from $1.86 till $2.10.</p>
<p>P&amp;U has already said that it will pay out a dividend for the fourth quarter of 1996 of $0.27.</p>
<p>In 1995 P&amp;U posted earnings per share of $1.34.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from Aros, Carnegie, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Enskilda, Fischer, Handelsbanken, James Capel, Kleinwort Benson, Matteus, Paribas, Swedbank, and Ohman.</p>
<p>P&amp;U's annual report will be released on February 26.</p>
<p>   (US$)		    AVG     RANGE	   ANALYSTS</p>
<p> Profit/share '96	 1.92    1.86-2.10	  12</p>
<p> Profit/share '97	 2.27    2.17-2.41	  12</p>
<p> Profit/share '98	 2.63    2.50-2.85	  12</p>
<p>-- Joel Dahlberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1007</p>
